msgstr "Safe Shutdown"

msgid "Status / Log"
msgstr "Status / Log"

msgid "Print Finished Notification"
msgstr "Print Finished Notification"

msgid "Fires once, on OctoPrint's own \"print done\" event - no polling or MQTT progress tracking needed. Typically used to trigger a WLED effect, light flash, or any other MQTT-driven notification."
msgstr "Fires once, on OctoPrint's own \"print done\" event - no polling or MQTT progress tracking needed. Typically used to trigger a WLED effect, light flash, or any other MQTT-driven notification."

msgid "Publish an MQTT notification when a print finishes"
msgstr "Publish an MQTT notification when a print finishes"

msgid "Topic"
msgstr "Topic"

msgid "Payload (on / off)"
msgstr "Payload (on / off)"

msgid "Payload sent, then reverted after the delay below."
msgstr "Payload sent, then reverted after the delay below."

msgid "QoS / Retain"
msgstr "QoS / Retain"

msgid "Retain"
msgstr "Retain"

msgid "Revert after (seconds)"
msgstr "Revert after (seconds)"

msgid "0 = never revert, stays on the \"on\" payload."
msgstr "0 = never revert, stays on the \"on\" payload."

msgid "Quiet Hours"
msgstr "Quiet Hours"

msgid "During this window, the finish notification, the finish light, and the shared-light-on-finish action are all suppressed. Plug-follows-light control below is unaffected."
msgstr "During this window, the finish notification, the finish light, and the shared-light-on-finish action are all suppressed. Plug-follows-light control below is unaffected."

msgid "Enable quiet hours"
msgstr "Enable quiet hours"

msgid "From / To"
msgstr "From / To"

msgid "Can cross midnight, e.g. 22:00 → 10:00."
msgstr "Can cross midnight, e.g. 22:00 → 10:00."

msgid "Per-Printer Finish Indicator Light"
msgstr "Per-Printer Finish Indicator Light"

msgid "A dedicated light/relay for this printer only, turned on when this printer finishes a print."
msgstr "A dedicated light/relay for this printer only, turned on when this printer finishes a print."

msgid "Turn on a light/relay when this printer finishes"
msgstr "Turn on a light/relay when this printer finishes"

msgid "Turn off after (seconds)"
msgstr "Turn off after (seconds)"

msgid "0 = don't auto turn off on a timer."
msgstr "0 = don't auto turn off on a timer."

msgid "Also turn off when a new print starts"
msgstr "Also turn off when a new print starts"

msgid "Disable if this light doubles as a general/manual light (e.g. a hardware button on the same relay) - otherwise starting a print always overrides a manual toggle."
msgstr "Disable if this light doubles as a general/manual light (e.g. a hardware button on the same relay) - otherwise starting a print always overrides a manual toggle."

msgid "Set topic (publish)"
msgstr "Set topic (publish)"

msgid "Plain text for most devices (WLED, Tasmota, HA-style switches). Some Zigbee2MQTT converters need JSON instead, e.g. {\"state\": \"ON\"}."
msgstr "Plain text for most devices (WLED, Tasmota, HA-style switches). Some Zigbee2MQTT converters need JSON instead, e.g. {\"state\": \"ON\"}."

msgid "Set payload (on / off)"
msgstr "Set payload (on / off)"

msgid "Independent window from the Print Finished tab's quiet hours - during this window, the finish light is suppressed."
msgstr "Independent window from the Print Finished tab's quiet hours - during this window, the finish light is suppressed."

msgid "Shared Work Light"
msgstr "Shared Work Light"

msgid "A light/relay shared across multiple printers, kept on as long as THIS printer (i.e. this PrintButler/OctoPrint instance is running - it shares power with the printer, so \"running\" already means \"powered\") OR any peer printer's topic reports \"on\". Each PrintButler instance runs this independently - list the other printers' plug state topics as peers."
msgstr "A light/relay shared across multiple printers, kept on as long as THIS printer (i.e. this PrintButler/OctoPrint instance is running - it shares power with the printer, so \"running\" already means \"powered\") OR any peer printer's topic reports \"on\". Each PrintButler instance runs this independently - list the other printers' plug state topics as peers."

msgid "Keep the shared light on while any tracked printer is powered"
msgstr "Keep the shared light on while any tracked printer is powered"

msgid "State topic (optional, self-heal)"
msgstr "State topic (optional, self-heal)"

msgid "JSON field to read the on/off value from (blank = plain-text payload). If set, PrintButler re-asserts \"on\" if something else switches it off while a printer is still running."
msgstr "JSON field to read the on/off value from (blank = plain-text payload). If set, PrintButler re-asserts \"on\" if something else switches it off while a printer is still running."

msgid "Peer printer topics"
msgstr "Peer printer topics"

msgid "One MQTT topic per line, plus the \"on\" value and the JSON field to read it from (blank = plain-text payload). Same format assumed for all peers."
msgstr "One MQTT topic per line, plus the \"on\" value and the JSON field to read it from (blank = plain-text payload). Same format assumed for all peers."

msgid "Watches the bed and nozzle temperature continuously - not just after a print - and once both stay below their thresholds for the confirm time while the printer isn't printing, runs the shutdown command below. This host can't cut its own mains power reliably (OctoPrint and MQTT die mid-shutdown), so instead PrintButler publishes a trigger topic first; wire a Home Assistant automation (or similar) to that topic to cut power once it confirms the host is actually down."
msgstr "Watches the bed and nozzle temperature continuously - not just after a print - and once both stay below their thresholds for the confirm time while the printer isn't printing, runs the shutdown command below. This host can't cut its own mains power reliably (OctoPrint and MQTT die mid-shutdown), so instead PrintButler publishes a trigger topic first; wire a Home Assistant automation (or similar) to that topic to cut power once it confirms the host is actually down."

msgid "Enable Safe Shutdown"
msgstr "Enable Safe Shutdown"

msgid "Bed / Nozzle threshold (°C)"
msgstr "Bed / Nozzle threshold (°C)"

msgid "Confirm for (seconds)"
msgstr "Confirm for (seconds)"

msgid "Both temperatures must stay at or below their threshold for this long, after having been seen above it, before shutdown fires."
msgstr "Both temperatures must stay at or below their threshold for this long, after having been seen above it, before shutdown fires."

msgid "Shutdown command"
msgstr "Shutdown command"

msgid "Runs on the OctoPrint host. Needs passwordless sudo for shutdown if using \"sudo\"."
msgstr "Runs on the OctoPrint host. Needs passwordless sudo for shutdown if using \"sudo\"."

msgid "Trigger topic (publish)"
msgstr "Trigger topic (publish)"

msgid "Published right before the shutdown command runs. Point a Home Assistant automation at this topic to cut mains power safely."
msgstr "Published right before the shutdown command runs. Point a Home Assistant automation at this topic to cut mains power safely."

msgid "Trigger payload (on / off)"
msgstr "Trigger payload (on / off)"

msgid "\"On\" is published right before shutdown; \"off\" is published back on the next startup, so a retained topic doesn't stay stuck \"on\" and your automation gets a clean signal the host came back up."
msgstr "\"On\" is published right before shutdown; \"off\" is published back on the next startup, so a retained topic doesn't stay stuck \"on\" and your automation gets a clean signal the host came back up."

msgid "Settle delay (seconds)"
msgstr "Settle delay (seconds)"

msgid "Wait this long after publishing the trigger before running the shutdown command, so the message has time to actually leave the host."
msgstr "Wait this long after publishing the trigger before running the shutdown command, so the message has time to actually leave the host."

msgid "Controlled live by the power button in the top navigation bar - armed by default on every OctoPrint start; click it to disarm for the current session (e.g. to keep the printer on after this print)."
msgstr "Controlled live by the power button in the top navigation bar - armed by default on every OctoPrint start; click it to disarm for the current session (e.g. to keep the printer on after this print)."

